questions.question_text:
The graph shown has horizontal asymptote $y=2$, passes through $(0,3)$, and decreases from left to right.
Which equation matches it?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-3.2, xmax=4.5, ymin=0, ymax=6, samples=120, clip=false, axis line style={-{Stealth}}, xtick={-2,2,4}, ytick={1,2,3,4,5}]
\addplot[thick, blue, <->, domain=-2:4.5] {exp(-x*ln(2))+2};
\addplot[dashed, red, domain=-3.2:4.5] {2};
\node[below] at (axis cs:3,2) {$y=2$};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*, blue] coordinates {(0,3)};
\node[above right] at (axis cs:0,3) {$(0,3)$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
